course: dictionary
lesson: 13473
title: Hyperactivity in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hyperactivity is a noun. It means being much more active, restless and full of energy than usual, so that sitting still is very hard. The «-ity» ending turns the adjective «hyperactive» into a noun, a name for the state. Hyper- means over or too much.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Mia could not sit still, and she kept jumping up to race around the room.» The restless racing is the clue: she has far more energy than usual. Everyone is very active sometimes, but hyperactivity is when it happens a lot and makes school or home harder.
explain: In medicine, hyperactivity is one part of ADHD, which stands for attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. «Sam has ADHD, and his doctor is helping him learn ways to focus.» ADHD is a real condition, not bad behaviour, and children with it can get help and often have great strengths.
explain: Science uses the word in a slightly different way. «The gland showed hyperactivity, making far more hormone than the body needed.» Here it means an organ or gland working too much. The same idea of "more than normal" still fits. Check any meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: Hyperactivity means much more active, restless and full of energy than usual.
fact: Hyperactivity is part of ADHD: attention deficit hyperactivity disorder.
fact: ADHD is a real condition, not bad behaviour, and children with it can get help.
fact: In science, «hyperactivity» can mean an organ or gland working too much.
fact: Myth: sugar causes hyperactivity. Studies have mostly not found this.
exercise: «Mia could not sit still, and she kept racing around the room.» What does this show? | Calm, quiet thinking | Being fast asleep | *Much more energy and restlessness than usual | Reading a book in silence
exercise: Hyperactivity is part of which condition? | A common cold | A type of sugar | Bad behaviour that a child chooses | *ADHD, a real condition that affects attention and activity
exercise: Ben says hyperactivity is just naughty behaviour. What is the best answer? | *ADHD is a real condition, not bad behaviour, and children can get help | Hyperactivity means being very quiet | Yes, it is always a choice the child makes | Yes, sugar is the only cause
test: «The gland showed hyperactivity.» In science, what does this mean? | A type of medicine | *An organ or gland working too much | An organ that has stopped working | A gland that is very small
test: Which is the best meaning of hyperactivity? | Being very good at maths | Feeling sad and quiet | Being very tired all day | *Being much more active, restless and full of energy than usual
exam: Jake says sugar causes hyperactivity. What do studies mostly show? | Sugar always makes children hyperactive | Studies prove sugar is the only cause | *Studies have mostly not found that sugar causes hyperactivity | Sugar stops hyperactivity
